The '''Bolto''' is a [[Tenno]] secondary that fires piercing bolts with a noticeable travel time.

This weapon can be sold for {{cc|5,000}}, it is also a [[weapon crafting ingredient]] for {{Weapon|Akbolto}} (x2) and {{Weapon|Hystrix}}.
{{Checklist|nocategory=true|
* {{Weapon|Bolto}} + {{Weapon|Bolto}} → {{Weapon|Akbolto}}<br><small>Akbolto required for [[Akjagara]]</small>
* {{Weapon|Bolto}} + {{Weapon|Viper}} → {{Weapon|Hystrix}}
}}

==Characteristics==
*This weapon deals primarily {{D|Puncture}} damage.
*Can use the Bolto-exclusive {{M|Entropy Spike}} mod.

{{Advantages|}}
{{Disadvantages|}}

{{WeaponComparison|Akbolto}}

==Acquisition==
The Bolto's blueprint can be purchased from the [[Market]].

{{BuildAutomatic|type=Weapon}}

==Notes==
*Bolts pin killed enemies to walls or floors.
*Bolto can puncture a container and has a 100% chance to destroy the container behind it. The {{Weapon|Akbolto}} does not have this capability.
*Upon release, the Bolto created no noise when fired, making it SILENT, but in its upgrade section of the [[Arsenal]] its noise level was listed as ALARMING. This was because enemies may still be alerted if the player hits the ground around the target. This was a bug and is no longer the case as of {{ver|Specters of the Rail 2.2}}, Bolto (along with Akbolto and Telos Akbolto) are now ALARMING at all times.
*Unlike its [[Akbolto|akimbo variant]], the Bolto doesn't have a prime version.

==Tips==
*Higher fire rate can be achieved by tapping the trigger at specific intervals, not quickly tapping the trigger, as the fire rate will be lower.
**Pacing shots allows the Bolto to recover from a shot's muzzle climb, improving the accuracy of the following shot.
*The innate {{Pol|Vazarin}} polarity can somewhat limit elemental modding potential, thus making it a less desirable polarity for elemental modding. If you wish to focus more on elemental damage, then it is recommended to either ignore the polarity or use [[Forma]] to turn it into a more suitable polarity.

