{{Codex|The Boltor is an automatic rifle that rapidly fires heavy bolts that can pin your foes to the walls.}}

The '''Boltor''' is a {{Faction|Tenno}} assault rifle with the characteristic of firing bolt projectiles instead of conventional bullets. This weapon requires the user to take into account projectile travel time while aiming at targets, as well as the projectile drift, making the Boltor difficult to use effectively beyond medium ranges.

This weapon can be sold for {{cc|7,500}}. This weapon is a [[weapon crafting ingredient]] for {{Weapon|Boltace}}.
{{Checklist|nocategory=true|
* {{Weapon|Kronen}} + {{Weapon|Boltor}} → {{Weapon|Boltace}}
}}

==Characteristics==
*This weapon deals primarily {{D|Puncture}} damage.
*Bolts fired stick to their target, and will fling bodies on kill.
**The body will damage targets in its path.
**Corpses can be pinned to terrain.
{{Advantages|*Flung bodies help in dealing with crowds.
*Low recoil.}}

{{Disadvantages|*Projectiles have travel time with slight arcing.}}

{{WeaponComparison|Telos Boltor}}
{{WeaponComparison|Boltor Prime|header=n}}

==Acquisition==
The Boltor's blueprint can be purchased from the [[Market]]. Alternatively, a built Boltor is awarded from completing the [[Venus]] to [[Mercury]] [[Junction]], complete with a free weapon slot and pre-installed [[Orokin Catalyst]].

{{BuildAutomatic|type=Weapon}}

==Incarnon Genesis==
{{Transclude|Boltor Incarnon Genesis#Acquisition}}

{{Transclude|Boltor Incarnon Genesis#Incarnon Genesis}}

==Tips==
*Use the {{M|Rifle Ammo Mutation}} mod to gain extra ammo if needed, or alternatively bring along [[Squad Ammo Restore]]. Carrier's {{M|Ammo Case}} is also a good option.
**Alternatively, bring along a good sidearm/melee weapon if you find yourself in a situation with no ammo.
**Mods like {{M|Ammo Drum}} can also help with ammo efficiency problems.
*The bolts, like the {{Weapon|Kunai}}, stagger enemies, making it useful for mild crowd control.
*With the slow travel time and high rate of fire, the Boltor can sometimes hit an enemy with four or five bolts at once, after a Tenno has disengaged from fighting that target to recover shields/health or to move to another objective.

==Trivia==

*Originally the weapon shared the same icon and description as {{Weapon|Braton}}, while the blueprint icon and in-game model shared that of {{Weapon|Burston}}. As of a visual update on February 8, 2013, it now has a unique appearance and description.

